I'd hate to rain on your parade, but that number there is not Movement.
It is Magic Resistance.  If I recall the AD&D definition, this is a number
which says how likely a monster is to resist a spell cast by a character
of its same level (?).  As a result, magic is considerably less effective
on Archons than it is on gray dragons.  Funny how that is, if the
gray dragon hide gives you a protection?

>Also note it's incredible high speed.  In fact only the Wizard
>and the Mail Deamon are faster than an Archon.

To amend this.  The Wizard is more Magic Resistant, just to make him
more of a pain.  The mail daemon is set to the largest signed-char
integer (127), just so he doesn't get killed.  I notice that you've
omitted the several named demons who have higher numbers as well.

To rectify the Speed situation,
   Dragons have a speed factor of 9
   Archons have a speed factor of 12
   Bats have a speed factor of 20-22
   Air elementals have a speed factor of 36

Perhaps the Archons seem fast to you because they have so
many attacks per round.  Not to mention that one almost never
encounters Archons singly.

Moral:  If you're going to refer to spoiler data or source file
info to support your point, please be sure that you're correctly
interpreting the data you present!  :)  Some of these monsters
which have a Magic Resistance of zero, I really wish they had a
Movement Rating of zero!!!

